From: Gordon Kessler
To: All
Subj: I ran my program on an ARM/AT
Date: 03-14-90 00:30

I'll say this once, and quietly, and then we'll never speak of it.

At the SFARM meeting on Tuesday (I go to spy, everyone knows this),
Karen Whitfield put a floppy in her ARM/AT and ran MY program, a genuine
x86 .COM file I wrote myself in 1986, under this ELBOW thing.  The X86
lamp on the front panel came on, amber, and stayed on.  My program ran.
Every instruction of it.  Correctly.

Then she ran a benchmark, the same C program compiled once for the ARM
and once for the 8086, and ran both.  I'm not going to say what the
numbers were.  I'm going to say that I went home and did not turn on
the 386 that night.

That's all.  That's the whole message.

Gordon
